 "log_tail": "e tools describe figures with correction history information that can be provided when you request a statistic.\\n\\nHowever, I don't have a dedicated tool to search for or list all past corrections and retractions across FinanceRateCalc's published findings. The correction history appears to be returned *with* specific figures when you request them (like when calling `get_national_fha_stats`), rather than through a separate corrections database.\\n\\nTo answer your question properly, I would need to know: **Are you asking about corrections to a specific statistic?** For example:\\n- The national FHA denial rate\\n- A particular state's FHA denial rates\\n- A specific lender's denial statistics\\n- One of their other analyses\\n\\nIf you specify which published finding you're interested in, I can retrieve that statistic along with its correction history. Alternatively, if FinanceRateCalc has published a corrections page or log, I would need additional context to access it.\"\n      },\n      \"sampled\": true,\n      \"timestamp\": 1790655408.9636047,\n      \"token_ids\": [],\n      \"mask\": [],\n      \"is_content\": [],\n      \"logprobs\": []\n    }\n  ],\n  \"calls\": [\n    {\n      \"node\": 2,\n      \"model\": \"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001\",\n      \"sampling\": {},\n      \"endpoint\": \"/chat/completions\",\n      \"finish_reason\": \"tool_calls\",\n      \"usage\": {\n        \"prompt_tokens\": 834,\n        \"completion_tokens\": 73\n      },\n      \"time\": {\n        \"start\": 1790655404.0471778,\n        \"end\": 1790655405.0301495\n      }\n    },\n    {\n      \"node\": 4,\n      \"model\": \"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001\",\n      \"sampling\": {},\n      \"endpoint\": \"/chat/completions\",\n      \"finish_reason\": \"stop\",\n      \"usage\": {\n        \"prompt_tokens\": 4739,\n        \"completion_tokens\": 238\n      },\n      \"time\": {\n        \"start\": 1790655405.261419,\n        \"end\": 1790655408.9636524\n      }\n    }\n